    "turn_idx": 25,
    "turn_text": "you go. A couple of questions quickly because I want to be sensitive to your time. What's possible? Just quickly in the politics of the bill, on the one hand, I would think you have hope. Midterms made clear that voters are concerned about health care and costs and the candidates who didn't understand that. They didn't do so good, did they? Your committee also has shown the ability, I think you just had an opioid bill passed. So your committee has shown the ability to get done bipartisan legislation. On the other hand, you may be aware that there's not much other evidence that Republicans and Democrats are finding common ground and being supportive, et cetera. So are you hopeful, can your bill cut through? Can something get done?",
