    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/5/0/50327.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 31,
    "turn_text": "and Governmental Affairs and Immigration. It's pretty evident to this point that Trump and Republicans have used the border and immigration issue to whip up their base. That was part of what was discussed around the midterm election. However, it's equally clear, at least in my opinion, that, and you'll correct me if you disagree, of course, that Democrats need a clear policy and message on border security. And at this point, it's not clear that the party has got a message that has gotten through. So do you feel, one, that the Democrats have a clear message on border security and immigration, if not, What should it be? And if you do feel like they do have a message, why does it seem to get drowned out?",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
    "explicit_propositions": [
      {
        "text": "Trump and Republicans have used the border and immigration issue to energize their political base.",
        "confidence": 0.95
